# Web UX contract

Follow `docs/ux/web-ux-conventions.md` (source of truth). Digest:

- Operator UX: attention/lists over charts; progressive disclosure; thumb-zone CTAs (bottom nav, FAB sheet, detail bars).
- Feedback ladder: snackbar = soft success/validation; dialog = money/destructive settle; sheet = choose action / search. Errors: explain · suggest next · preserve input · no stack traces.
- Bottom nav: Home, Transactions, Resources, Customers, More. Do not add/remove tabs without updating the conventions doc.
- Transactions = Orders + cash Loans in the UI only; keep rentals and money_loans engines separate.
- FAB always includes Search, New Order, Return, Add Resource, Scan. Search = Home typeahead + FAB modal (not a route).
- Status colors: Available green, Rented blue, Due Today orange, Overdue red, Archived grey. Customer Trusted/Standard use `TierPill` (never status pills); subscription = compact meta.
- Offline: subtle non-blocking banner only; never gate workflows. More-tab offline toggle is demo only.
- Appearance: Dark/Light only; default Dark; More segmented toggle; M3 seed `#006D77` via `AppTheme`; ColorScheme over light-only hardcodes. No system theme / third high-contrast theme. A11y: ADR-007 (WCAG 2.2 AA).
- Home defaults: search + KPIs + needsAttention (Customize Home for optional modules; FAB for New Order / Return).
- Forms: items-first New Order; commercial step only when policy requires/offers; money notes never block settle; return/cancel = confirm dialogs.
- Money note: optional free text ≤20 (`kMoneyNoteMaxLength`) on Pay / New Order commercial / loan create & cash entries / return-cancel.
- Search: first non-empty trimmed character (`kMinMeaningfulTextLength = 1`); no min-length helper under search fields. Order notes (append-only) still ≥3.
